      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Student Life: Career Services - Elms College eTOOLS Application Portal Alumnae Library Blazer Book Link ElmsConnect Email IT Service Desk Moodle Student Dashboard | REQUEST INFO | VISIT | APPLY | GIVE Skip to content Elms College Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Certificate Programs Online CE Programs Off Campus Programs School of Nursing Academic Resources Centers and Institutes Center for Student Success Browse by Major & Minor Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions Center for Equity in Urban Education (CEUE) International Admissions Transition from Anna Maria College Kirley School of Continuing Education Tuition & Financial Aid Virtual Tour Student Life Commencement Residence Life Spiritual Life Alumnae Library Campus Bookstore Campus Ministry Career Services Commuter Resources Dean of Students Health and Counseling Centers International Programs Office Registrar Student Accommodations and Support Services (SASS) Student Engagement and Leadership Athletics Alumni Alumni Association Board Alumni News, Social Media, and Publications Alumni Services Distinguished Alumni Award In Memoriam Alumni Reunion Support Elms About Elms Administrative Offices Campus Map Contact Us Governance Mission and Core Values Partnerships Public Safety Quick Facts Strategic Plan (FY 2025-FY 2027) Student Stories Viewbook Virtual Tour Visit Elms College Working at Elms College I Am A: Prospective Student Accepted Undergraduate Student Accepted Continuing Education Student Current Student Graduate Student International Student Prospective Nursing Student Transfer Student Alumni Faculty Parent Veteran Search for: Search Button Search Search for: Apply Give Academics ❯ Center for Student Success ❯ Career Services Career Services About Us Students Alumni Faculty and Staff Welcome! Career Services helps you every step along your path to career success. We will help you explore who you are, find real, work-related experience, and prepare you for a successful job search. Learn more about career services a Elms College from J Marshall, Director of Career Services. Career Fair Highlights: Real Connections. Real Outcomes. At Elms, career preparation is part of the experience from day one. See how our students build connections and practice professional skills at our annual Career Fair. ElmsConnect Career Services Meet the Staff “Employers actually seek out Elms College students.” –  J Marshall, Director of Career Services. Did You Know: 100% of education majors are currently employed (class of 2019) 91% of the class of 2024 are employed or continuing their education 90% of our master’s degree graduates are currently employed (class of 2024) Visit Us Hours: Career Services is open Monday through Friday, 8:30am – 4:30pm. Please note that we are closed on holidays aligned with Elms College, some breaks, and occasionally for staff development and training. Directions: Getting to Career Services on the Elms College campus is easy! Our address is: 291 Springfield St. Chicopee, MA 01013 We are located in the Center for Student Success in the Alumnae Library. View Larger Map Share this: Inquire Visit Apply Discover Your Purpose 413-594-2761 291 Springfield Street Chicopee, MA 01013 Stay Connected with Us Social Media Directory Resources 🎓Commencement ▷ Academics Academic Calendar Information Browse by Major/Minor Info Sessions Library Online Continuing Education Programs & Certificates School of Nursing Scholarships The Elms Promise Tuition & Financial Aid ▷ Students & Faculty Center for Student Success Current Students ElmsConnect Faculty & Staff Dashboard Moodle ▷ Institutional Info Accreditation Employment Partnerships Title IX - Request for Information - (for Nursing): Open Form Close Notice Of Nondiscriminatory Policy As To Students Elms College admits students of any race, color, national, and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © College of Our Lady of the Elms Sitemap | Title IX | Privacy Policy | Contact Webmaster | Equal Opportunity Policy"
